# Read by kitty's open-actions matcher on top of Python's mimetypes table —
# the 3.14 stdlib kitty bundles plus macOS's /etc/apache2/mime.types, which
# every Python reads at init. That table has no entry for Kotlin, Gradle,
# Svelte, .tsx, .properties or .zsh, and the Apache lines file .rs under
# application/rls-services+xml and .ts under video/mp2t — so a `mime text/*`
# rule alone would hand those to macOS `open`. One type per line, then its
# extensions; a later entry overrides the table's. .yml is not here: the
# stdlib knows it as application/yaml, which kitty remaps to text/yaml.
text/x-kotlin kt kts
text/x-gradle gradle
text/x-rust rs
text/x-svelte svelte
text/typescript ts tsx
# .sql is not missing from the table — it is MISLABELLED, and differently from
# .rs and .ts: macOS's Apache lines file it under application/x-sql, which is
# not in the set kitty remaps to text/*, so without this line a click on one
# leaves kitty entirely.
text/x-sql sql
text/x-properties properties
text/x-shellscript zsh
